            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "We should probably make this title less terse also."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I cleaned this up and simplified a lot.  PTAL."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm very hesitant to merge this commit.  These kind of statements have legal ramifications.\n\nThe TSC exists because of the Charter of the project, which has been delegated from the Linux Foundation as the holder of the project's assets.  The charter exclusively gives the TSC \"governance of the project\".\n\nThe TSC has _delegated_ the day to day, technical administration of the project to the TOF.  That was done when the TSC voted on (and approved) the TOF \"contract\": https://github.com/openbmc/docs/blob/master/tof/contract.md .  @bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com spearheaded that effort.\n\nIf the project wants to disband the TSC for the project governance, we have to approach Linux Foundation about a change to the Charter.  I have absolutely no idea what that entails since the original Charter was established within \"key companies\", many of whom do not have representation on the TOF."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I can remove this statement from the commit message if that helps to just make this about the readme?  This section includes a bunch of people that haven't participated for a while, so (at least to me) it didn't make sense to put that on the top level readme.  This wasn't about disbanding the TSC at all.\n\nOr is there something more you're concerned about?  Maybe we just give a pointer to the charter?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "ok, ironically our charter link on the website 404s now \ud83d\ude0a\n\nhttps://openbmc.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/62/2018/03/charter_openbmc_02142018.pdf"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "> I can remove this statement from the commit message if that helps to just make this about the readme? \n\nThe important thing, I think, is that we avoid talking about \"governance\".  That's more of a legal term.\n\nI also gave a minor phrase to insert.  That makes it clearer on the delegated responsibilities, I think.\n\nHonestly, I'd like to fully disband the TSC as well but we'd have to start that conversation with LF."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I removed the term governance, and accepted your suggestion.\n\nI agree with you about disbanding the TSC (or maybe getting TOF renamed as TSC) but that's not what this commit is about.  This is just making sure our top level readme points to somewhere that people can get actual technical input."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "README.md",
                    "line": 193,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I think if we add a qualifier like this I'd be more keen.\n\n```suggestion\nThe Technical Oversight Forum (TOF) guides the technical direction of the project. Members are voted on by\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "README.md",
                    "line": 193,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Fix applied."
                }
            ],
